# Eco Translator

> Part of [LoPAS Open Translator Core](../LoPAS-Open-Translator-Core)

Translates ecosystem and biodiversity data into common state space.

---

## Data Sources

| Source | Data | Update |
|--------|------|--------|
| GBIF | Species occurrence, biodiversity index | Periodic |
| Sentinel (ESA) | Vegetation health (NDVI), land use | 5 days |
| EM-DAT | Disaster frequency, historical impact | Event-driven |

---

## Schema

```yaml
meta:
  translator: eco-translator
  version: 0.1.0
  timestamp:
  lag_seconds:
  coverage_gap:
  confidence:

coordinate:
  lat:
  lon:
  timestamp:

sources:
  - provider: GBIF
    update_interval: 604800   # weekly
  - provider: Sentinel
    update_interval: 432000   # 5 days
  - provider: EM-DAT
    update_interval: 86400

observation:
  biodiversity_index:         # species richness score
  vegetation_health:          # NDVI 0.0–1.0
  land_use_change_pct:        # % change from baseline
  disaster_frequency:         # events per year in region
  invasive_species_presence:  # true/false

derived:
  resilience:                 # 0.0–1.0
  habitat_stability:          # 0.0–1.0
  recovery_capacity:          # 0.0–1.0
  fragmentation_index:        # habitat connectivity

state:
  status:                     # SAFE | CAUTION | WARNING | CRITICAL
  vulnerability_score:        # 0.0–1.0
  trend:                      # IMPROVING | STABLE | DEGRADING | UNKNOWN

lopas:
  TRS:    # ecosystem resonance / vitality
  EFI:    # entropy-fertility — biodiversity as creative diversity
  AHI:    # adaptive harmony — recovery capacity
  SCI:    # accumulated disaster stress

action:
  recommendation:             # MONITOR | PROTECT | RESTORE
  confidence:
```

---

## Note on Slow Data

GBIF and EM-DAT update slowly.  
Sentinel updates every 5 days.  
High `lag_seconds` here is normal — not an error.

When `coverage_gap: true` alongside `SCI` elevation,  
it may indicate disaster impact in an unobserved zone.

